Publish single-user statistics synchronously instead of scheduling SIGALRM.

The delegated runtime correctly refuses setitimer until signal delivery exists.
A standalone backend can publish its statistics before reading the next command;
there is no need for a deferred idle wakeup. Statement/transaction/lock timeouts
still require real signal support and are not claimed by this port.

--- a/src/backend/tcop/postgres.c
+++ b/src/backend/tcop/postgres.c
@@ -4666,7 +4666,14 @@
 				 * performance impact. That's OK because pgstat_report_stat()
 				 * won't have us wake up sooner than a prior call.
 				 */
+				/* A single-user Capstone backend has no asynchronous signal
+				 * delivery yet. Flush statistics synchronously, so no idle
+				 * SIGALRM is needed to publish deferred statistics. */
+#ifdef __CAPSTONE__
+				stats_timeout = pgstat_report_stat(!IsUnderPostmaster);
+#else
 				stats_timeout = pgstat_report_stat(false);
+#endif
 				if (stats_timeout > 0)
 				{
 					if (!get_timeout_active(IDLE_STATS_UPDATE_TIMEOUT))
